{
  "Title": "ELSA-2026-500688: openssl security update (MODERATE)",
  "Description": "[1:1.1.1k-19]\n- Fix CVE-2026-54872: Private key recovery via timing side-channel in generic elliptic curve\n  Resolves: RHEL-272648\n- Fix CVE-2026-35189: Denial of Service via excessive memory allocation in CRL distribution\n  Resolves: RHEL-272752\n- Fix CVE-2026-75806: Denial of Service via undersized DTLS record\n  Resolves: RHEL-272764\n\n[1:1.1.1k-18]\n- Fix CVE-2026-63072: heap buffer overflow in CMS key unwrapping\n  Resolves: RHEL-246293\n- Fix CVE-2026-84782: DTLS Retransmits Handshake Messages From a Stale Buffer Offset\n  Resolves: RHEL-264416\n\n[1:1.1.1k-17]\n- Fixes CVE-2026-28390: Denial of Service due to NULL pointer dereference in CMS EnvelopedData processing\n  Resolves: RHEL-165759\n\n[1:1.1.1k-16]\n- Fix CVE-2026-45447: Heap Use-After-Free in OpenSSL PKCS7_verify()\n  Resolves: RHEL-179623\n- Fix CVE-2024-4741: Use After Free with SSL_free_buffers\n  Resolves: RHEL-39119\n\n[1:1.1.1k-15]\n- Fix CVE-2025-69419: Arbitrary code execution due to out-of-bounds write in PKCS#12 processing\n  Resolves: RHEL-142010\n\n[1:1.1.1k-14]\n- Backport fix for Out-of-bounds read \u0026 write in RFC 3211 KEK Unwrap\n  Fix CVE-2025-9230\n  Resolves: RHEL-128613\n- Fix bug for ticket_lifetime_hint exceed issue\n  Resolves: RHEL-119891",
